  <tr><td><strong>Luol Deng</strong></td><td>Sudan/UK</td><td>Small Forward</td><td>2× NBA All-Star; played 14 NBA seasons</td></tr>
  <tr><td><strong>Serge Ibaka</strong></td><td>Congo/Spain</td><td>Center/Power Forward</td><td>3× NBA All-Defensive Team; 2019 NBA Champion</td></tr>
</table>

<div class="highlight">
  <strong>Nigerian Basketball:</strong> Nigeria’s national basketball teams (D’Tigers for men, D’Tigress for women) have grown significantly in recent years. In 2021, the D’Tigers defeated USA, Argentina, and Australia in pre-Olympic warm-up games — a landmark achievement for African basketball. The D’Tigress reached the 2020 Olympics and were the first African team to qualify for the FIBA Women’s Basketball World Cup.
</div>

